float Health;"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Remote Procedure Calls (RPCs)"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"RPCs are functions that execute on a remote machine. Unlike variables that synchronize continuously based on state, RPCs are event-driven and execute specific logic across the network boundary."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Server RPCs: Executed on the client, run on the server. Used for player actions like firing a weapon or opening a door."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Client RPCs: Executed on the server, run on a specific client. Used for targeted events like awarding points or triggering UI notifications."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Net Multicast RPCs: Executed on the server, run on the server and all currently connected clients. Use sparingly for visual effects like explosions."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"UFUNCTION(Server, Reliable, WithValidation)
void Server_PerformAction();"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Implementing Replication in C++"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"To enable networking on an Actor or ActorComponent, you must override the GetLifetimeReplicatedProps function to register your replicated variables."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"void AMyCharacter::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(TArray<FLifetimeProperty>& OutLifetimeProps) const
{
    Super::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(OutLifetimeProps);
    DOREPLIFETIME(AMyCharacter, Health);
}"},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mastering the client-server model, utilizing proper variable replication, and structuring RPCs securely are foundational pillars for building stable and scalable multiplayer games in Unreal Engine."}]
